<title>USA: Fox to release Independence Day video Nov 22.</title>
<headline>Fox to release Independence Day video Nov 22.</headline>
<dateline>CENTURY CITY, Calif. 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twentieth Century Fox studios Tuesday said it plans to release its popular summer film &quot;Independence Day&quot; on videotape on November 22, just in time for the holidays.</p>
<p>In a statement, the News Corp unit said the video, which smashed box office records this summer, will sell for $22.98 in the United States and $24.98 in Canada.</p>
<p>The alien adventure film has already grossed more than $268 million at the box office.</p>
<p>Fox said it plans to launch the video with an extensive marketing campaign.</p>
</text>
